# examples/regressions/current_region_stack — the §16 arena crumb D fixture
# (`docs/design/plano-s16-runtime-prelude-injection.md` §3/§6 RF5). The behavioural proof for the
# Teko arena's current-region stack (`region_enter`/`region_leave`/`alloc`/real `region_current`) that
# crumb D adds to `src/runtime/arena.tks`: it exercises enter-a-child / alloc-lands-in-child / leave /
# alloc-lands-in-root / drop-the-child over the raw mmap `fundo`, mirroring the C twin's
# `cur_regions`/`cur_rsp` semantics (`teko_rt.c` `tk_region_enter`/`tk_region_leave`/`tk_alloc`).
# Exit 42 on all-pass; any other code names the invariant that broke.
#
# A SELF-CONTAINED promoted probe (its own local `src/arena.tks` copy of the Teko arena core, extended
# with the crumb D current-region stack, and its own `src/sys/sys.tks` mirror of the `SYS_*`/`PROT_*`/
# `MAP_*` consts), because the real `teko::sys` and `teko::runtime` live in the COMPILER's own
# reserved-root project a standalone project has no visibility into (the `arena_mmap` precedent). The
# `teko::sys::syscall*` and `teko::mem::load_u64`/`store_u64` INTRINSICS are compiler builtins reached
# under their `teko::`-rooted names; only the numbers/flags come from the local mirror. Validating the
# current-region stack on the C leg BEFORE the L2 flip (crumb E) is why the promoted probe exists — the
# real `arena.tks` is still DORMANT.
name = "current_region_stack"
source = "src"

